# OptimizedDE.db is generated at container startup (see main.py's
# ensure_optimized_db()) - it should never be baked into the image from
# whatever happens to be sitting in a local dev copy of db/, or a
# stale/incomplete one gets shipped and the app skips rebuilding it
# (this actually happened once: a stray 0-byte file locally became a
# tableless "optimized" db in the image, and the app crashed on boot).
db/OptimizedDE.db
# Bind-mounted at runtime (docker-compose.yml), not baked into the
# image - it's 3GB and the whole point of the bind mount is a rebuild
# never has to re-copy that. Missed the first time this was set up:
# COPY . ./ was quietly baking it in anyway since nothing here excluded
# it, doubling the image size for nothing - the container never actually
# read that copy, since the bind mount overlays it with identical
# content at startup regardless.
db/voice_archive.db
.git
__pycache__
test
logs
